What is adapted from it here, rewritten (internal/controlplane/listening/linkedin.go, issue #1291): the Posts search
address and its datePosted facet (linkedin_mcp_server/linkedin/search_urls.py), the script that pairs each rendered
post with its own URN by its boundary (linkedin/feed.py FEED_POST_BOUNDARIES_JS), the post's permalink form and URN
pattern (linkedin/feed_payload.py), the media player's noise lines (linkedin/text.py), the sign-in, challenge and
account-restriction routes (core/auth.py) and the throttling statuses 429 and 999 (core/throttle.py). Changed: the
script runs on the search page and returns the page's address, navigation status and empty state with the posts;
the recording of each response's status by the call that sent its request (core/throttle.py) is rewritten as a
browser context's record of its tab's requests (internal/controlplane/browser/contexts.go).
